note right of HttpServer
  Routes (all require
  Authorization: Bearer <token>):
  POST   /communities
  GET    /communities
  PATCH  /communities/{id}              (owner only)
  DELETE /communities/{id}              (owner only)
  POST   /communities/{id}/join
  POST   /communities/{id}/moderators   (owner only, issue #114)
  DELETE /communities/{id}/moderators/{login} (owner only)
  GET    /communities/{id}/moderators
  POST   /communities/{id}/channels
  GET    /communities/{id}/channels
  PATCH  /channels/{id}      (channel owner, community
                              owner, or community moderator)
  DELETE /channels/{id}      (same authority as PATCH)
  GET    /channels/{id}/messages
  POST   /channels/{id}/attachments
  GET    /attachments/{id}
  GET    /channels/{id}/messages/search
                             (?q=, limit=20; 400 for
                             an encrypted channel —
                             issue #138, nothing to
                             search server-side)
  GET    /communities/{id}/members      (issue #138)
  PUT    /channels/{id}/keys/{login}    (issue #138, channel
                              owner, community owner, or
                              community moderator only)
  GET    /channels/{id}/keys/me         (issue #138, 404
                              if no key set for you yet)

  Owner-only routes answer 403 for
  non-owners, 404 for a nonexistent
  id — MutationResult keeps those
  two cases distinct end-to-end.

  Attachments (issue #116, up to
  kMaxAttachmentSizeBytes = 5 MB):
  upload body is {"filename",
  "content_type", "data_base64"} —
  400 on missing fields, invalid
  base64, or oversized payload,
  else 201 with the new id. Download
  decodes the stored base64 and
  writes raw bytes, filename in a
  sanitized Content-Disposition
  header (CR/LF/'"' stripped —
  header-injection guard).

  Search (issue #118): plain
  case-insensitive substring test
  (position(lower(q) in lower(body))
  > 0), not full-text search — no
  ranking/stemming, a first-version
  simplification. Missing/empty
  'q' is 400. Newest match first.

  E2E encryption Phase 2 (issue
  #138): Channel.isEncrypted is set
  only at creation. This server
  never sees a raw channel key or
  plaintext body for an encrypted
  channel — messages.body is
  ciphertext the client produced,
  relayed/stored as opaque TEXT
  exactly like a plaintext channel's
  body (no schema difference).
  channel_keys holds one wrapped
  copy of the channel's symmetric
  key per member, sealed with that
  member's own X25519 public key
  (client-side crypto_box_seal) —
  setChannelKey()'s authority is the
  same owner/moderator check as
  renameChannel()/deleteChannel(),
  since only whoever already holds
  the raw key could have produced a
  valid wrapped copy in the first
  place. A member who joins after
  creation has no key until the
  owner/moderator wraps one for
  them — no automatic re-wrap on
  join. Search and attachment
  upload (POST /channels/{id}/
  attachments) are both rejected
  (400) for an encrypted channel in
  this phase — attachments aren't
  encrypted client-side yet.
end note

note right of WebSocketServer
  Protocol per connection:
  1st frame: {"token", "channel_id"}
  after that, key-presence dispatch
  (checked in this order):
    {"call_join": true}
      -> {"call_roster": [...]} to
         sender, {"call_peer_joined"}
         to other call participants
    {"call_leave": true}
      -> {"call_peer_left"} to the
         remaining call participants
         (same on Close/Error without
         an explicit leave)
    {"call_signal": {"to","payload"}}
      -> relayed verbatim as
         {"call_signal": {"from",
         "payload"}} to that one
         participant's socket, or
         {"error": "peer not in
         call"} to the sender
    {"typing": true}
      -> {"user_typing": "<login>"}
         to every other *chat*
         subscriber (issue #96,
         never echoed back to sender)
    {"edit_message": {"id","body"}}
      -> (issue #107) only the
         message's own author may
         edit it — {"error": ...}
         to the sender on 404/403,
         else {"message_edited":
         {"id","body","edited_at"}}
         broadcast to every *chat*
         subscriber
    {"delete_message": {"id"}}
      -> wider than edit_message
         (issue #114): the author,
         channel/community owner, or
         a community moderator may
         delete — {"message_deleted":
         {"id"}} broadcast on success
    {"body", "attachment_id"?} (fallback)
      -> (issue #116) attachment_id
         optionally references an
         attachment already uploaded
         via POST /channels/{id}/
         attachments; broadcast to
         every *chat* subscriber of
         that channel with
         attachment_id/
         attachment_filename fields
         (null when there's none)

  Call participants (callParticipants_)
  are a separate, per-channel presence
  set from *chat* subscribers
  (subscriptions_) — being subscribed
  to a channel's text chat does not
  imply being in its call, and vice
  versa. This server only relays call
  signaling (SDP/ICE payloads) — it
  never inspects "payload" contents.
  See issue #46.
end note

@enduml
